Students taught explicit critical thinking skills score 0.62 standard deviations higher on problem-solving assessments than control groups, according to a 2015 meta-analysis of 341 studies.
The Watson-Glaser Critical Thinking Appraisal, used by 80% of law schools in the US for admissions, predicts professional performance better than GPA alone.
PISA (Programme for International Student Assessment) results show that students from countries with enquiry-based science education score 30+ points higher on problem-solving — even controlling for national income.
